  "description": "Is the canonical cross-species nucleon ordering p...pn...n derivable, or a free degree of freedom? Q1: it is LIVE IN PRODUCTION -- the A>=3 binding chain (mass_table_comprehensive -> binding_canonical -> closed_form_tau_M -> closed_form_ratio) iterates a hardcoded ['p']*Z + ['n']*N, so every mixed-species A>=3 row of mass-table-comprehensive.witness.json inherits the choice. Q2: the interface product factorises as P(o)/P(canonical) = (f_pn/f_pp)^(b_p-1) * (f_pn/f_nn)^(b_n-1) over the p-/n-BLOCK counts; at the substrate anchor f_pn/f_pp < 1 < f_pn/f_nn, so the canonical arrangement is a SADDLE -- no extremal principle can select it (candidate 1 REFUTED). The trace IS a function of the interface multiset, but the multiset is not determined by (Z, N), so candidate 2 re-coordinatises the DOF without removing it. What survives is candidate 3: a genuine undeclared degree of freedom. free_parameters = 0; no AME quantity selects anything; nothing is wired; no ordering is recommended.",
